{
  "question": "Can exact whole-action ENABLED reuse continue past the one-million-closed-row cutoff within the same 8 MiB mask budget?",
  "issue": 1351,
  "method": "At up to 1,048,576 closed rows the complete source-presence index remains unchanged. Above that limit an aligned window contains up to 16,384 consecutive source masks (128 KiB). A new source window is read from the same checked physical original occurrences. Unknown producer labels, open rows, warning and ownership checks keep their previous fallback. Smaller earlier prefix checks can set a higher run-wide peak than the final window.",
  "hardware": "Dedicated AWS c7i.4xlarge, us-east-2, one logical worker; Intel Xeon Platinum 8488C; Ubuntu 24.04, Rust 1.99.0 release --locked. There were separate dedicated hosts for the production-only pair and the broader engineering comparisons.",
